import lib/cadkernel/brep_revolve_rational.dl

function check rational revolution {boolean:condition}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "abort", nothing)

function rational revolution near {a number:actual} to {a number:expected}:
    execute:
        check rational revolution ((the absolute value of (actual - expected)) < 1e-9)

set plane to the cad xy plane
set pivot to the cad zero vector3
set axis to the cad y axis
set ellipse to a cad ellipse at (a cad vector2 with x 3.0 and y 1.0) with radii 1.0 and 0.5 along (a cad vector2 with x 1.0 and y 0.0)
set piece to the cad curve2 of (a cad ellipse arc2 on ellipse from 0.0 to 3.141592653589793)
set profile to a list containing piece
set frame to the cad rational revolution turn of profile on plane about pivot along axis by 1.5707963267948966
check rational revolution frame's valid
check rational revolution (frame's radial's x > 0.0)
set swept to the cad rational revolution surface of piece on plane for frame
check rational revolution swept's valid
check rational revolution (swept's collapsed = false)
check rational revolution (swept's value's uDegree = 2)
check rational revolution (swept's value's vDegree = 2)
set onSurface to the cad point on swept's value at parameters 0.0 and 0.0
rational revolution near onSurface's x to 4.0
rational revolution near onSurface's y to 1.0
rational revolution near onSurface's z to 0.0
print "ellipse_revolution_is_exact_rational_surface" as a line

free profile
set piece to the cad curve2 of (the full cad ellipse arc2 on ellipse)
set profile to a list containing piece
set frame to the cad rational revolution turn of profile on plane about pivot along axis by 1.5707963267948966
check rational revolution frame's valid
set swept to the cad rational revolution surface of piece on plane for frame
check rational revolution swept's valid
check rational revolution swept's value's uClosed
check rational revolution (swept's value's vClosed = false)
print "closed_profile_preserves_source_periodicity" as a line

set controls to a list containing (a cad vector2 with x 1.0 and y 0.0)
append (a cad vector2 with x -0.1 and y 1.0) to controls
append (a cad vector2 with x 1.0 and y 2.0) to controls
set knots to a list containing 0.0
append 0.0 to knots
append 0.0 to knots
append 1.0 to knots
append 1.0 to knots
append 1.0 to knots
set weights to a list containing 1.0
append 1.0 to weights
append 1.0 to weights
set nurbs to the strict cad nurbs curve2 of degree 2 with controls controls, knots knots and weights weights
check rational revolution nurbs's valid
set piece to the cad curve2 of nurbs's value
free profile
set profile to a list containing piece
set frame to the cad rational revolution turn of profile on plane about pivot along axis by 6.283185307179586
check rational revolution frame's valid
set validFrame to frame
set swept to the cad rational revolution surface of piece on plane for frame
check rational revolution swept's valid
check rational revolution swept's value's vClosed

set axisControls to a list containing (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0)
append (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 2.0) to axisControls
set axisKnots to a list containing 0.0
append 0.0 to axisKnots
append 1.0 to axisKnots
append 1.0 to axisKnots
set axisWeights to a list containing 1.0
append 1.0 to axisWeights
set axisCurve to the strict cad nurbs curve2 of degree 1 with controls axisControls, knots axisKnots and weights axisWeights
check rational revolution axisCurve's valid
set axisPiece to the cad curve2 of axisCurve's value
free profile
set profile to a list containing (the cad curve2 of nurbs's value)
append axisPiece to profile
set frame to the cad rational revolution turn of profile on plane about pivot along axis by 1.5707963267948966
check rational revolution frame's valid
set omitted to the cad rational revolution surface of axisPiece on plane for frame
check rational revolution ((omitted's valid = false) and omitted's collapsed)
free profile
free axisControls
free axisKnots
free axisWeights
print "axis_collapsed_nurbs_piece_is_omitted" as a line
check rational revolution ((the length of swept's value's controls) = 3)
print "nurbs_hull_refines_and_full_turn_closes" as a line

replace item at index 1 in controls with (a cad vector2 with x -2.0 and y 1.0)
set crossing to the strict cad nurbs curve2 of degree 2 with controls controls, knots knots and weights weights
set piece to the cad curve2 of crossing's value
set profile to a list containing piece
set frame to the cad rational revolution turn of profile on plane about pivot along axis by 1.5707963267948966
check rational revolution (frame's valid = false)
set refused to the cad rational revolution surface of piece on plane for validFrame
check rational revolution (refused's valid = false)
print "nurbs_axis_crossing_is_refused" as a line

free controls
free knots
free weights
free profile
check rational revolution swept's value's vClosed
